Visualization Requirements:

Color scheme: Assign each unique eNodeB a distinct base color. Within that color, use darker shades for stronger RSRP and lighter shades for weaker RSRP, using LinearSegmentedColormap. Normalize RSRP values per eNodeB.
Voronoi-based coverage map: Compute a Voronoi diagram from all measurement point coordinates using scipy.spatial.Voronoi + shapely to clip cells to the bounding box. Fill each Voronoi cell with the serving eNodeB's color shaded by RSRP intensity.
Coverage overlap: For each Voronoi cell, if top_1–top_5 contain other eNodeBs, draw their colors as semi-transparent border halos (2–4px wide, ~30% opacity) around the cell edge, stacked by rank. This conveys overlapping coverage without cluttering the interior.
Base map: Render on top of an OpenStreetMap tile basemap using contextily.

